      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The current status of radionuclide imaging in the patients with cardiac disease has been reviewed. Currently it is possible to detect acute myocardial infarction, exercise-induced or spontaneous myocardial ischemia and ventricular function during rest or exercise in a relatively noninvasive manner. The recent development of mobile computer/camera systems opened the possibility for the study and evaluation of critically ill patients. Further developments of techniques and instrumentation can be expected in the near future."},
